# Dog API

> Dog data as a free JSON API: <%= number_with_delimiter @counts[:breeds] %> breeds, <%= @counts[:groups] %> groups and <%= number_with_delimiter @counts[:facts] %> facts, with <%= number_with_delimiter @counts[:images] %> pictures. No key and no sign up.

Every endpoint is a GET and none of them authenticate. Requests are capped at
<%= Rack::Attack::REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE %> a minute per IP. v2 answers in JSON:API format and is the version to
build on; v1 answers in a shape of its own and is deprecated. Collections page
with `page[number]` and `page[size]`. Pictures are served as a redirect to the
file, so an `<img>` tag can point straight at one, and each carries the licence
and the attribution its source asks for.

## Documentation

- [Which version to use](<%= request.base_url %>/docs): the difference between v1 and v2, and why v2 is the one to pick.
<% @documents.each do |document| -%>
